;; THE OFF SWITCH. This profile allows everything.
;;
;; It exists so that turning confinement OFF is a VISIBLE fact rather than an
;; invisible one. `metistry up` renders the reconciler's job with
;; `-f <profile>`; when METISTRY_RECONCILER_SANDBOX=0 that profile is this
;; file, and the difference is readable in the rendered plist, in
;; supervisor.json, in `metistry up --dry-run`, and in `metistry doctor`'s
;; `sandbox` row, which names the profile each child actually runs under.
;;
;; The alternative was two argv shapes for one job, which would have meant
;; either two plist templates or a shell string built at render time — the
;; exact defect class the 2026-09-10 launchd trial found. One argv, one
;; placeholder, one file that says what it does.
;;
;; WHY THE SWITCH EXISTS AT ALL. Confinement costs the reconciler its git
;; credential helper and its SSH remotes (ops/sandbox/reconciler.sb explains
;; both, with the measurements). An install whose remote it cannot push to
;; while confined must have a way back that is not "edit a profile", and
;; "the sole committer stopped backing up the vault" must never be the
;; failure mode of a security improvement.
;;
;; Do not point anything else at this file. If a component needs a wider
;; grant than its profile gives, widen the profile — one rule, reviewed —
;; rather than removing the boundary.

(version 1)
(allow default)
